What:		/sys/class/net/pon0/device/gpon_events
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Linux PON developers <netdev@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		GC1601 GPON diagnostic counters. DBRu fields are sampled by the
		O5 watchdog, normally once per second. Reading this file uses
		cached values and does not read or clear hardware counters.

		dbru_detected counts watchdog samples with a nonzero DBRu flag.
		dbru_busy counts flagged samples skipped because upstream traffic
		was at least 2 kbit/s. The first sample after entering O5 primes
		the measurement and performs no recovery.

		dbru_fixes is the legacy name for recovery passes, including
		passes where all T-CONT rewrites were skipped. It is not a count
		of successful repairs. Each pass pulses the vendor flag-clear
		register, preserving the existing recovery sequence.

		dbru_rewrites counts T-CONT report-load attempts.
		dbru_buffer_skips counts T-CONTs skipped for insufficient free
		buffers or an unavailable packet engine. dbru_qmu_errors counts
		failed queue-manager threshold helper calls.

		dbru_flag_clears counts passes whose immediate readback contains
		none of the original flags. dbru_flag_persists counts passes where
		any original flag remains. Clearing the latch does not prove
		that upstream traffic resumed; correlate byte counters and
		connectivity. A flag may also recur after this readback.

		dbru_last_before, dbru_last_rewritten, dbru_last_skipped and
		dbru_last_after are hexadecimal T-CONT masks for the last recovery
		pass. dbru_last_rate_kbps is that pass's integer upstream rate
		in bits per millisecond. These last-pass fields remain unchanged
		when a later sample is unflagged, busy or only primes the timer.

		Counters accumulate over the lifetime of the driver instance.
